@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title Host shell → Go: retire every bash script the operator's Mac executes
' purpose: remove macOS /bin/bash 3.2 from every host code path
' would touch: defs/lib/docker-build.sh, defs/*/build.sh, defs/*/ensure.sh (deleted)
' would touch: defs/*/test.sh, defs/*/tests/*.sh, defs/lib/{test-image,egress}.sh (deleted P3; in-image command strings kept in internal/imagetest)
' would touch: internal/imagetest/** (P3's Go suites)
' would touch: lib/*.sh, scripts/*.sh, mise.toml (lib/*.sh and scripts/*.sh deleted P4)
' would touch: internal/maintain/** (BuildPlan, DeployPlan, TestPlan), cmd/proveo/provision.go
' would touch: internal/imagebuild/targets.go (the build table; P2 put it here, not in harness.manifest)
' would touch: internal/contract/{agent_pin,image_resolution,host_bash,installer_bash,git_hooks}_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo-dev/**
' covers: internal/installtest/**
' covers: internal/contract/host_bash_test.go
' covers: internal/contract/installer_bash_test.go
' covers: scripts/githooks/post-commit
' covers: mise.toml
' session: 92196ee8-2438-4fda-ac25-7311bf16c563
' PLANNED 2026-09-22. P1–P4 LANDED 2026-09-22 — plan complete.
' Decided by the operator over fish (no errexit, non-POSIX at every
' Kit/sbx/Dockerfile/installer boundary) and over a mise-pinned bash 5
' (provision.go ran `bash build.sh` for END USERS, who get 3.2, until P2).
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── MEASURED 2026-09-22, BEFORE P2: WHERE THE SHELL RAN ───────────────────
'   host build   defs/lib + build.sh + ensure.sh   ~1.2k lines   macOS 3.2
'   host libs    lib/*.sh + scripts/*.sh           ~0.6k lines   macOS 3.2
'   def tests    defs/*/tests/*.sh HARNESS         ~3.3k lines   macOS 3.2
'   in-image     packages/lib + entrypoints        ~3.8k lines   Debian bash 5
'   installer    apps/cli/public/cli/install.sh                  `curl | bash`, stock 3.2
' The def tests were first filed as in-container; they are not. helpers.sh
' sourced docker-build.sh (later the slim defs/lib/test-image.sh; both are
' deleted), fell back when `timeout` was missing, and drove `docker run … bash -c "<cmd>"` FROM the
' host. Only <cmd> runs inside.
' End users reached host bash too: cmd/proveo/provision.go ran
' `bash <def>/build.sh` when an image was missing. P2 removed that path.
'
' ── WHAT STAYS SHELL, AND WHY (final, after P4) ────────────────────────────
' In-image bash: it only ever meets bash 5, and sbx Kit startup commands, `sbx
' exec … bash -c` (internal/sbx/run.go) and Dockerfile RUN lines speak it.
' Lives under defs/ and packages/lib/.
' The installer: apps/cli/public/cli/{install,uninstall}.sh run on a machine
' that has no proveo yet (`curl | bash`), so they stay bash, GUARDED (P4).
' scripts/githooks/post-commit: git executes a hook FILE, so a 6-line POSIX
' `#!/bin/sh` shim cds to the repo root and execs
' `mise exec -- go run ./cmd/proveo-dev hooks post-commit`.
' The <cmd> strings inside internal/imagetest: they execute in the image.
' Fixture workspaces (e2e/testdata/, e2e/samples/): an agent operates on them.
'
' ── PHASES (each one ships green and deletes what it replaces) ─────────────
' P1  internal/imagebuild — the docker-build.sh primitives in Go: agent version
'     pin (npm / pypi / github), image ref + resolve + require-published, buildx
'     builder ensure + driver choice, pull policy, cache flags, registry-DNS
'     help, browser variant. The contract tables that exec those shell
'     functions are ported as Go unit tests; the shell tests STAY until P2
'     deletes the shell, because build.sh still runs it. Image resolution
'     already lives in Go (internal/maintain.ResolveImage).
'     LANDED 2026-09-22 as internal/imagebuild. Deliberate differences:
'       * `-t repo` with no tag is `:latest` and refused for --load; the
'         shell's `${a##*:}` returned the whole ref and let it through.
'       * npm reads the registry JSON (NPM_CONFIG_REGISTRY honoured) rather
'         than `npm view`; pypi needs no python3 fallback.
'       * output goes through internal/ui (Notef/Warnf/Failf), not emoji.
' P2  declarative build — each def's variants, Dockerfile, base, build-args and
'     parent chain move into a `build:` block in harness.manifest.
'     maintain.BuildPlan / DeployPlan and provision.go call imagebuild directly.
'     PARITY GATE before deletion: for every target and variant, the buildx
'     argv Go renders equals the argv the old script ran (golden, --print).
'     Then build.sh, ensure.sh and docker-build.sh are deleted.
'     LANDED 2026-09-22. Every defs/*/build.sh, defs/*/ensure.sh and
'     defs/lib/docker-build.sh is deleted.
'       * DEVIATION: the recipes live in a Go table, internal/imagebuild/
'         targets.go `Specs` (Repo, Override, Dockerfile, Context, Parent,
'         Needs, Layer, Pins, EnvArgs, Floor), not in a harness.manifest
'         `build:` block. 6 of the 16 registry targets (the four bases, the
'         two sidecars) have no manifest to hold one, and
'         TestEverySpecIsARegistryTarget pins the table to maintain.Registry.
'       * ensure = push → RequirePublished; present + Floor ok → done;
'         present without Floor → rebuild; absent → pull, else build. Each
'         Floor is the in-image `sh -c` probe its ensure.sh used to run.
'       * PARITY: internal/imagebuild/parity_test.go + testdata/
'         build_argv.golden, 48 cases (16 targets x --load, --push, cold
'         host; 83 buildx invocations), written
'         while build.sh and BuildTarget rendered identical buildx argv.
'       * maintain: Target.BuildScript/BuildArgs gone, Target.RepoRoot added;
'         BuildPlan/DeployPlan emit `imagebuild <target> --tag T [--push]
'         [--no-cache]` as an in-process Command.Run step.
'       * BUG FIXED (provision.go): the end-user fallback ran `bash build.sh`
'         with no args, which defaulted to :latest and was refused for --load.
'         It now builds the image's target at :local when asked for :latest
'         (buildTag) and hands the run that ref; PreflightImages returns the
'         image it settled on.
'       * PROVEO_<X>_IMAGE names the target's repo; --tag sets the tag.
'       * FINDING: codex is NOT pinned. CODEX_VERSION is an EnvArg defaulting
'         to `latest`, exactly as its build.sh did; parity kept it, and
'         agent_pin_test does not cover codex. Recorded in
'         _spec/_devops/agent-version-pin.puml.
'       * The def tests keep a slim defs/lib/test-image.sh (proveo_ref_tag,
'         proveo_image_created, proveo_resolve_image, proveo_test_image)
'         until P3.
' P3  def tests → Go — the TOOLS/CONFIG arrays are already tables; they become
'     `-tags=image` table tests. A context deadline replaces `timeout`/
'     `gtimeout`. test.sh and tests/*.sh are deleted; TestPlan runs go test.
'     LANDED 2026-09-22 as internal/imagetest.
'       * FRAMEWORK: internal/imagetest/imagetest.go — Resolve (env override,
'         then maintain.ResolveImage), New (skips an absent image), Suite
'         with Success/Failure/Contains/Matches/Inspect/Skip/Check, and Docker
'         bounded by a context timeout in place of run_timeout / timeout /
'         gtimeout. Each check is its own subtest named by its description.
'       * SUITES: internal/imagetest/{claudecode,codex,cursor,opencode,cecli,
'         mitmproxy,detached_smoke}_test.go, build tag `image`, one
'         TestImage<Def> each. defs/lib/test-image.sh, defs/lib/egress.sh,
'         e2e/docker-detached-smoke.sh, defs/tests/run_contract_tests.sh and
'         defs/tests/test_harness_contracts.sh are deleted with them.
'       * maintain.TestPlan: Target.Suite = base name of DefDir; the step is
'           go test -tags=image -count=1 -v -run '^TestImage<Def>$' ./internal/imagetest/
'         so `proveo test <target>` and `mise run test-defs` run Go.
'       * PARITY GATE, per check description, against :local images with no
'         provider keys set (pass/fail/skip):
'           claudecode 220/0/6 · codex 47/0/1 · opencode 60/0/8
'           cursor 55/1/1, then 54/0/1 after the one dropped check
'         cecli, mitmproxy and the detached smoke print few or no per-check
'         lines, so their parity is exit status: all pass.
'       * FINDING: cursor's shell suite aborted at check 21 (exit 127) and
'         never ran phases 3–6 (security, config, defaults, llm). "[browser]
'         bun (from proveo/base-node) runs TypeScript" ran `bun` in
'         cursor-browser, which layers onto the bun-free cursor image (check
'         14 asserts that absence). assert_output_contains called docker_exec
'         unguarded under `set -e`. The operator DROPPED that check from
'         cursor's suite; opencode's twin stays. In Go one failing check
'         cannot hide the rest (_spec/tests/testing-strategy.puml).
'       * GAP: claudecode's provider checks sourced defs/lib/egress.sh, which
'         ran the proveo-egress binary. ccEgress (claudecode_test.go) calls
'         provider.Detect and egress.ProviderAllowConf directly instead. The
'         binary also reads PROVEO_EGRESS_ENV_FILE; the port ignores it, so
'         that input has no image-suite coverage.
'       * Only the <cmd> strings survive, verbatim, inside the Go files; they
'         still run in the image under Debian bash 5.
' P4  lib/ + scripts/ — ui/registry/helpers callers and go-test-coverage.sh /
'     stage-cli-cdn.sh become Go (subcommands or `go run` mise tasks).
'     LANDED 2026-09-22. Operator decisions:
'       1 delete defs/*/run.sh and mitmproxy's run.sh / debug.sh;
'         `proveo run <target>` is the interface.
'       2 maintainer tooling lives in cmd/proveo-dev, a SEPARATE binary that
'         never ships: goreleaser lists its binaries explicitly and
'         proveo-dev is absent.
'       3 the installer stays bash but guarded; its test runner becomes Go.
'       * COMMAND MAP (cobra; each tool self-registers from its own file):
'           coverage {unit|merge|coverage|integration|e2e|all}  scripts/go-test-coverage.sh
'           stage-cdn                    scripts/stage-cli-cdn.sh
'           build-cli [--release]        mise build-cli body
'           deploy-cli · dev-cli         mise deploy-cli / dev-cli bodies
'           ladder · idle                mise ladder-all / idle-all bodies
'           e2e-full                     mise test-e2e-full body; runs e2e,
'                                        then idle, then ladder in-process
'           debug [target] [--tag T] [--print]
'                                        mise debug body + lib/{ui,helpers,
'                                        registry}.sh; registry in-process via
'                                        manifest.Load + maintain.Registry
'           lint                         mise lint body
'           hooks install|post-commit    scripts/githooks/install + the
'                                        post-commit body
'           firehol-ipsets               defs/sidecars/squid-proxy/
'                                        update-firehol-ipsets.sh (ported, not
'                                        dropped: docker-egress still runs squid)
'           render-subagents <harness> [dest]
'                                        defs/lib/render-subagents.sh; runs the
'                                        in-image render_subagents in the
'                                        harness image, working-tree
'                                        entrypoint-lib.sh mounted, --network none
'       * BEHAVIOUR CHANGE: `debug` with no target on a non-TTY stdin fails
'         with "Missing target." plus the list; the bash silently picked base.
'       * mise.toml: every task body is one command (`go run ./cmd/proveo-dev
'         lint`, `go run ./cmd/proveo build`, …). test-images and
'         test-images-sbx are arrays: stage-cdn, the installer suite, the image
'         suites. `ci` is a single printf.
'       * INSTALLER: internal/installtest/install_test.go (TestInstallScripts,
'         23 checks, no build tag, runs in ci) replaces apps/cli/public/cli/
'         tests/run_tests.sh. It stages its own CDN unless
'         PROVEO_INSTALLTEST_CDN names one.
'       * FINDING: the old runner went through `env bash` and met Homebrew
'         bash 5 on a maintainer Mac, so it never proved 3.2. The Go suite
'         runs install.sh / uninstall.sh under /bin/bash (3.2.57) on darwin.
'         internal/contract/installer_bash_test.go adds `/bin/bash -n` and a
'         bash-4-feature scan on both scripts; it found no violations.
'       * DELETED: defs/{cecli,claudecode,codex,cursor,opencode}/run.sh,
'         defs/sidecars/mitmproxy/{run,debug}.sh, lib/{ui,helpers,registry}.sh,
'         scripts/go-test-coverage.sh, scripts/stage-cli-cdn.sh,
'         scripts/githooks/install, defs/lib/render-subagents.sh,
'         defs/sidecars/squid-proxy/update-firehol-ipsets.sh,
'         apps/cli/public/cli/tests/run_tests.sh. The contract tests
'         TestRunShimsExecProveo and TestMiseTasksUsingBashSyntaxDeclareBash
'         went with them.
'       * RE-POINTED contract tests: git_hooks_test.go reads
'         cmd/proveo-dev/hooks.go + the POSIX shim, builds proveo-dev and
'         installs into a temp git repo; TestLadderAllDetectsOnlyATopLevelSkip
'         reads cmd/proveo-dev/ladder.go; TestE2EFullIsTheSilentDeathGate reads
'         mise.toml + cmd/proveo-dev/{idle,e2efull}.go.
'       * CECLI_IMAGE was documented but read by nothing; the docs dropped it.
'
' ── THE GATE THAT FINISHES IT (LANDED P4) ──────────────────────────────────
' internal/contract/host_bash_test.go replaces TestHostScriptsAvoidBash4Builtins.
' TestNoHostShellOutsideTheAllowlist: every tracked `*.sh` or shell-shebang
' file sits under an in-image / fixture tree (defs/, packages/lib/,
' e2e/testdata/, e2e/samples/) or in hostShellAllowed, each entry with its
' reason: install.sh, uninstall.sh, scripts/githooks/post-commit. A stale
' allowlist entry fails too. Mutation-checked: a staged scripts/stray.sh fails.
' TestMiseTasksRunNoShellScripts: mise.toml holds no bash shebang, no
' `bash scripts/`, no `run = """` block. A mise body is one command, so the
' old dash-vs-bash shebang rule has nothing left to check.

rectangle "operator's Mac" as MAC <<host>> {
  component "proveo build / provision\nexec bash build.sh — BEFORE P2" as NOW <<error>>
  component "internal/imagebuild\nGo — LANDED P2" as GO <<app>>
  component "go test -tags=image\ninternal/imagetest — LANDED P3" as GT <<app>>
  component "cmd/proveo-dev\nmaintainer tools, not shipped — LANDED P4" as DEV <<app>>
  component "host_bash_test.go\nallowlist gate — LANDED P4" as GATE <<app>>
}
rectangle "image (Debian)" as IMG <<host>> {
  component "packages/lib + entrypoints\nbash 5 — stays" as INIMG <<app>>
}
component "install.sh / uninstall.sh\nguarded bash — stays" as INST <<app>>

NOW ARROW_ERROR GO : replaced, parity-gated
GO ARROW_MAIN IMG : docker buildx
GT ARROW_MAIN IMG : docker run <cmd>
DEV ARROW_MAIN GO : proveo build / test
INST ARROW_MAIN MAC : bootstraps proveo
GATE ARROW_OPTIONAL INST : allowlisted

note right of NOW
  **End users hit this path.**
  provision.go ran `bash build.sh`
  on a missing image, so a fix for
  contributors alone left them on 3.2.
end note

note bottom of GO
  **Parity before deletion.**
  48 golden cases matched each old
  build.sh argv, per target and
  mode, before the scripts went.
end note

note bottom of GT
  **One check, one subtest.** A failure
  stays local, where `set -e` once hid
  four of cursor's phases; a context
  deadline replaces macOS's missing
  `timeout` binary.
end note

note right of DEV
  **Separate binary, never shipped.**
  goreleaser lists binaries by name;
  proveo-dev is absent, so maintainer
  tools stay off the CDN.
end note

note bottom of GATE
  **The allowlist is the finish line.**
  A new host *.sh outside defs/,
  packages/lib/ or e2e fixtures fails
  unless it names its reason.
end note

note right of INIMG
  **Never meets 3.2.**
  Kit startup, `sbx exec bash -c`
  and Dockerfile RUN speak it, so
  moving it would add a boundary
  instead of removing one.
end note

note right of INST
  **Runs before proveo exists.**
  `curl | bash` on a stranger's box;
  its Go suite runs /bin/bash 3.2 on
  darwin, not Homebrew's bash 5.
end note
@enduml
